# Woodwork and Test Lab badges — checked against official scouting.org excerpts.

@owner mb.woodwork
@complete partial
@note Requirements 5 and 6 were not visible in the excerpts and are not outlined yet.
@desc Woodwork teaches safe, skilled work with wood: shop safety and the Totin’ Chip, how lumber is grown, milled and graded, caring for and sharpening tools, building useful projects from your own drawings, and careers in woodworking.
@safety Wear eye and hearing protection and a dust mask, keep tools sharp, and use power tools only with adult supervision.
1 k! Safety :: Woodworking hazards, first aid, eye, hearing and dust protection, and the Totin’ Chip.
2 a Wood :: How timber is grown and milled and how lumber is cured and graded, and collecting useful woods.
3 demo Tools :: Caring for and storing tools and sharpening cutting tools.
4 a A woodworking project :: Building a useful project from your own drawings with hand tools.
7 a Careers :: Talking with a cabinetmaker or finish carpenter about the trade.

@owner mb.auctioneering
@desc Auctioneering (a Test Lab badge) combines public speaking and salesmanship: how auctions work, the auctioneer’s chant and the skills of running a sale.

@owner mb.life-skills
@desc Life Skills (a Test Lab badge) covers practical independence: health, household management, money, getting ready for a job, and everyday tasks such as sewing on a button.

@owner mb.physics
@desc Physics (a Test Lab badge) explores how matter, energy and motion behave. Its trial requirements are published on the Scouts BSA Test Lab page.

@owner mb.sewing-needlework
@desc Sewing & Needlework (a Test Lab badge) teaches basic hand and machine sewing through several small, practical projects, including hand stitching and appliqué.

@owner mb.dance
@desc Dance (a Test Lab badge) explores movement and performance. Its trial requirements are published on the Scouts BSA Test Lab page.

@owner mb.psychology
@desc Psychology (a Test Lab badge) explores how people think, feel and behave. Its trial requirements are published on the Scouts BSA Test Lab page.

@owner mb.citizenship-in-society
@note Scouting America discontinued this badge effective February 27, 2026, so no requirement outline is published.
@desc Citizenship in Society focused on diversity, equity, inclusion and ethical leadership. Scouting America discontinued it effective February 27, 2026, and it is no longer required for Eagle.
